# Interaction_Design — Skeleton

## 1. Applies when
Puzzle or systemic games built on object interaction (puzzle_adventure).

## 2. This document owns
- The interaction verb table: verbs (push/burn/freeze/...), their subjects, results and stacking rules.
- Interaction affordance rules (how the player reads what is interactable).
- Verb-vs-material matrix (fire melts ice, etc.) and its exceptions.

## 3. This document does NOT own
- UI presentation of prompts — UI_UX_Design.
- Puzzle instances using the verbs — Puzzle_Design.
- Physics implementation parameters — Technical_Design.

## 4. Recommended chapter structure
1. Verb philosophy / 2. Verb table / 3. Materials & states / 4. Verb-material matrix / 5. Stacking & priority / 6. Affordance rules / 7. Open questions

## 5. Common boundaries
- Interaction vs Puzzle: mechanics toolkit here, authored challenges in Puzzle.
- New verbs require a row here before any puzzle may use them.

## 6. Common audit rules
- Matrix cells are exhaustive: every verb x material cell is defined or explicitly N/A.
- No puzzle references an undeclared verb.
